{
 "result": "csvsum.py is a single-pass Python reader: it reads all of stdin as bytes, splits on newlines, skips the header, splits each line on commas, sums val per cat in a dict with float, then writes the cats sorted with %.2f sums. It passes the public sample (in-0 matches out-0, SAME) and was accepted by assay at baseline median 2.0881 with 6.1% noise. Two micro-optimized variants (defaultdict, no per-line empty check) scored 2.071 and 2.061, below the incumbent, so the colony kept the current body. I am resting because the remaining cuts are per-line overhead changes that the noise floor makes hard to distinguish, and further gains would need a different approach such as bulk parsing, which I have not tested.",
